      {
        "id": "kestrel-overnight",
        "heading": "Kestrel Porch Cam: one night on battery",
        "text": [
          "Source: the reviewed Kestrel Porch Cam overnight design, and the product manager's answers. Why did a customer get a low-battery alert in the night, and why did the package alert come late when their Wi-Fi was down?",
          "The camera checks in with the Kestrel cloud every 30 minutes with its battery level. The low-battery alert is sent once, when a check-in reports 20% or less, and not again until the battery is back above 30%. Animal clips are saved without an alert. A Wi-Fi outage of about 10 minutes does not mark the camera offline; that takes 60 minutes without a check-in.",
          "Clock times are approximate or illustrative. The design's rough power figures (about 1% an hour plus 1% per clip) would reach 20% nearer 2:30 AM than the 4 AM alert shown, so the battery is held at 25% until 4 AM rather than calculated. After that it follows the design's figures: about 1% an hour on battery, about 3.5% an hour on solar."
        ],
